        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Cross link  color (property) and color() (function) and <color> (type) See also's]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40880</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40880"/>
        <updated>2025-08-25T20:56:41.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1761395?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">The <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/color_value/color" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">color()</code> (<code class="notranslate">color_value/color</code>)</a> is currently the top result for the query <a href="https://duckduckgo.com/?q=site%253Adeveloper.mozilla.org+color" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">color site:developer.mozilla.org</code> on DDG</a>, and I've observed there is no clear organic path to (intended) <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/color" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">color</code> property (<code class="notranslate">CSS/color</code>)</a> from there, what "See also" seems fit.</p>
<hr>
<h5 dir="auto">Motivation</h5>
<p dir="auto">I am (ab)using DDG's "bang" («I'm feeling lucky»") feature through a keyword search to get to MDN references as quickly as possible, and <code class="notranslate">https://duckduckgo.com/?q=!%20site:developer.mozilla.org%20color</code> kicked me to a page I was not expecting, though, arguably, has more "color" keywords in the URL than any other page.</p>
<h5 dir="auto">Additional details</h5>
<p dir="auto">Also, I have the "See also" section pulled up before main content with userstyle, because quite often continuing elsewhere related is what I am coming for.  That's why I've hit addressed issue and why it knocked me off.</p>]]></content>
